{"type":"plan","title":"The Red Kite","logline":"A torn kite, a grandfather's seam, and a golden star lift a child's heart above Brighton's waves.","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Wide shot of Brighton seafront at morning wind: Maya stands on the pier, red kite soaring high above the railings, sea glittering, golden light.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"On a windy autumn morning in Brighton, eight-year-old Maya flies her red kite above the pier.","cites":[]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Medium shot close to pier railings as a sudden gust slams the kite into the wood, the red sail rips from corner to corner, a jagged hole flaps, sky shows through.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"A gust slams it into the pier railings, and the red sail tears from corner to corner.","cites":[]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Pan","description":"Pan along the shingle beach as Maya runs toward home, the torn kite hugged to her chest, wind tugging her coat.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs home along the seafront, the broken kite hugged to her chest.","cites":[]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close-up inside grandfather's kitchen, morning light through window, grandfather looks up from newspaper, curious.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Her grandfather, who mended sails when he was young, looks up from his newspaper.","cites":[]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Slow zoom-in","description":"Slow zoom-in on wooden table as grandfather lays the torn kite flat, threads a needle with sailcloth thread, steady hands.","mode":"still","dialogue":"At the kitchen table he lays the kite flat and threads a needle with sailcloth thread.","cites":[]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close-up of grandfather's hands stitching a sailor's seam, each stitch pulls the torn edges together, Maya watches intently.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Stitch by stitch, he shows Maya how a sailor's seam holds against the wind.","cites":[]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Slow zoom-in","description":"Slow zoom-in on Maya's fingertips painting a big gold star on the white patch, the star glints in the morning light.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya paints a small gold star over the patch, so the kite will remember.","cites":[]},{"index":8,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Wide shot of Brighton seafront in afternoon, Maya and grandfather walk side by side along the sand, kite tucked under grandfather's arm, beach huts colorful.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"In the afternoon they walk back to the beach together, the kite under Grandfather's arm.","cites":[]},{"index":9,"shotType":"Low angle","description":"Low angle shot from the sand as Maya runs into the wind, the starred kite lifts higher than ever over rolling waves, string taut.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs into the wind, and the kite climbs higher than ever over the waves.","cites":[]},{"index":10,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Medium shot from behind Maya as she hands the string to grandfather, he laughs like a boy, kite dancing in the breeze.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"She hands the string to her grandfather, and he laughs like a boy.","cites":[]},{"index":11,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Wide shot at golden dusk, Maya and grandfather stroll home along the shoreline, the mended kite rests on Maya's shoulder, sea calm, lantern glow from pier.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"At golden dusk they walk home along the sand, the mended kite on Maya's shoulder.","cites":[]}]}
